WEBVTT

00:03.840 --> 00:04.080
Okay.

00:04.080 --> 00:07.000
So now we're going to go and extend our data flow diagram.

00:07.000 --> 00:08.960
But this time for the gold layer.

00:09.000 --> 00:14.120
So now let's go and copy the whole thing from the silver layer and put it over here side by side.

00:14.200 --> 00:17.520
And of course we can go and change the colouring to the gold.

00:17.560 --> 00:20.040
And now we're going to go and rename stuff.

00:20.160 --> 00:22.520
So this is the gold layer.

00:22.520 --> 00:25.000
But now of course we cannot leave those tables like this.

00:25.040 --> 00:27.080
We have completely new data model.

00:27.080 --> 00:27.760
So what do we have.

00:27.800 --> 00:30.720
Over here we have the fact sales.

00:30.720 --> 00:33.440
We have dimension customers.

00:33.440 --> 00:36.480
And as well we have dimension products.

00:36.840 --> 00:39.320
So now what I'm going to do I'm going to go and remove all those stuff.

00:39.320 --> 00:41.200
We have only three tables.

00:41.200 --> 00:44.240
And let's go and put those three tables somewhere here in the center.

00:44.280 --> 00:47.800
So now what we have to do is to go and start connecting those stuff.

00:47.800 --> 00:52.720
I'm going to go with this arrow over here direct connection and start connecting stuff.

00:52.800 --> 00:55.800
So the sales details goes to the fact table.

00:55.840 --> 00:57.400
Maybe put the fact table over here.

00:57.400 --> 00:59.480
And then we have the dimension customer.

00:59.840 --> 01:02.720
This comes from the CRM customer info.

01:02.720 --> 01:05.640
And we have two tables from the ERP.

01:05.760 --> 01:07.490
It comes from this table as well.

01:08.010 --> 01:10.330
And the location from the ERP.

01:10.370 --> 01:13.290
Now the same thing goes for the products.

01:13.610 --> 01:18.290
It comes from the product info and comes from the categories from the ERP.

01:18.330 --> 01:20.370
Now as you can see here we have cross arrows.

01:20.370 --> 01:25.330
So what we can do we can go and select everything and we can say line jumps with a gap.

01:25.330 --> 01:28.890
And this makes it a little bit better in the visual for the arrows.

01:28.890 --> 01:33.850
So now for example if someone asks you where the data come from for the dimension products, you can

01:33.890 --> 01:37.890
open this diagram and tell them, okay, this comes from the server layer.

01:37.890 --> 01:43.650
We have like two tables, the product info from the CRM and as well the categories from the ERP and

01:43.650 --> 01:46.130
those server tables comes from the bronze layer.

01:46.130 --> 01:51.050
And you can see the product info comes from the CRM and the category comes from the ERP.

01:51.210 --> 01:52.250
So it is very simple.

01:52.250 --> 01:57.730
We have just created a full data lineage for our data warehouse from the sources into the different

01:57.730 --> 01:59.130
layers in our data warehouse.

01:59.130 --> 02:04.130
And data lineage is really amazing documentation that can help not only your users, but as well the

02:04.130 --> 02:04.690
developers.

02:04.730 --> 02:08.370
All right, so with that we have very nice data flow diagram and a data lineage.

02:08.490 --> 02:08.930
All right.

02:08.930 --> 02:10.810
So we have completed the data flow.

02:10.850 --> 02:15.780
It's really feel like progress, like achievements as we are clicking through all those tasks.

02:15.820 --> 02:20.100
And now we come to the last task in building the data warehouse, where we're going to go and commit

02:20.100 --> 02:21.980
our work in the GitHub repo.

02:25.900 --> 02:28.140
Okay, so now let's put our scripts in their project.

